# Why the sky is blue and sunsets red
subtitle: "How one effect, air scattering blue light far more than red, paints the daytime sky blue and turns the setting sun orange and red."

## Why the sky is blue and sunsets red
domain:
    x:
      - 400
      - 700
    'y':
      - 0
      - 10
    box:
      x: 620
      'y': 160
      w: 350
      h: 220

    shape sky #2f6b8f shape circle x 300 y 388 radius 238 style.fill #2f6b8f style.opacity 0.22 hidden true
    shape air dashed #8f887c shape circle x 300 y 388 radius 238 hidden true
    shape earth #3d3833 shape circle x 300 y 388 radius 195 style.fill #e6dcc6 hidden true
    label l_air "Air" left attach_to air hidden true
    text l_earth "Earth" #8f887c x 300 y 368 hidden true
    shape sun #d0865f shape circle x 880 y 610 radius 45 style.fill #f2c14e hidden true
    label l_sun "Sun" right attach_to sun hidden true
    text l_white "white" #8f887c x 700 y 585 font_size 28 hidden true
    path noon_out #b9b2a4 points [[838,593.9],[522.3,473.1]] style.stroke_width 5 hidden true
    path noon_in #b9b2a4 points [[522.3,473.1],[490.5,460.9]] style.stroke_width 5 hidden true
    group noon_beam members ["noon_out","noon_in"] hidden true
    shape noon_you #3d3833 shape circle x 482.1 y 457.7 radius 10 style.fill #3d3833 hidden true
    label l_noon "Noon" below-right attach_to noon_you hidden true
    shape m1 #3d3833 shape circle x 474.9 y 514.8 radius 10 style.fill #8f887c hidden true
    shape m2 #3d3833 shape circle x 514.8 y 410.4 radius 10 style.fill #8f887c hidden true
    shape m3 #3d3833 shape circle x 436.1 y 555.7 radius 10 style.fill #8f887c hidden true
    shape m4 #3d3833 shape circle x 415.9 y 588.6 radius 10 style.fill #8f887c hidden true
    shape m5 #3d3833 shape circle x 385.9 y 587.2 radius 10 style.fill #8f887c hidden true
    shape m6 #3d3833 shape circle x 355.9 y 585.8 radius 10 style.fill #8f887c hidden true
    group molecules members ["m1","m2","m3"] hidden true
    path s1 #2f6b8f points [[475.9,506.9],[480.6,469.6],[484.1,480],[480.6,469.6],[474.6,478.8]] style.stroke_width 3.5 hidden true
    path s2 #2f6b8f points [[510.3,417],[488.9,447.8],[490.6,437],[488.9,447.8],[498.5,442.4]] style.stroke_width 3.5 hidden true
    path s3 #2f6b8f points [[439.5,548.5],[477,468.6],[477.1,479.6],[477,468.6],[468.5,475.5]] style.stroke_width 3.5 hidden true
    group sky_scatter members ["s1","s2","s3"] hidden true
    shape dusk_you #3d3833 shape circle x 291 y 582.8 radius 10 style.fill #3d3833 hidden true
    label l_dusk "Sunset" above-left attach_to dusk_you hidden true
    path dusk_1 #b9b2a4 points [[835,607.9],[427.3,589.1]] style.stroke_width 5 hidden true
    path dusk_2g #b9b2a4 points [[427.3,589.1],[390.9,587.4]] style.stroke_width 5 hidden true
    path dusk_3g #b9b2a4 points [[390.9,587.4],[301,583.3]] style.stroke_width 5 hidden true
    path dusk_2 #d0865f points [[427.3,589.1],[390.9,587.4]] style.stroke_width 5 hidden true
    path dusk_3 #b5482e points [[390.9,587.4],[301,583.3]] style.stroke_width 6 hidden true
    group dusk_beam members ["dusk_1","dusk_2g","dusk_3g"] hidden true
    path d1 #2f6b8f points [[413.9,596.6],[401.9,636.6],[398.9,622.1],[401.9,636.6],[412.3,626.2]] style.stroke_width 3.5 hidden true
    path d2 #2f6b8f points [[383.9,595.2],[371.9,635.2],[368.9,620.7],[371.9,635.2],[382.3,624.8]] style.stroke_width 3.5 hidden true
    path d3 #2f6b8f points [[353.9,593.8],[341.9,633.8],[338.9,619.3],[341.9,633.8],[352.3,623.4]] style.stroke_width 3.5 hidden true
    group dusk_scatter members ["m4","m5","m6","d1","d2","d3"] hidden true
    text l_1x "1× air" x 610 y 545 font_size 30 hidden true
    text l_38x "38× air" x 385 y 675 font_size 30 hidden true
    axes ax x_label Wavelength y_label Scattering hidden true
    curve ray #3d3833 expr (700/x)*(700/x)*(700/x)*(700/x) hidden true
    label l_ray above attach_to ray tex "\\propto 1/\\lambda^4" hidden true
    dot p_violet #8a5fa8 at.on ray at.x 410 hidden true
    label l_violet "Violet" right attach_to p_violet hidden true

    card title "Blue sky, red sunset"

Why is the sky blue, and why do sunsets turn red?
    draw earth l_earth air l_air

Sunlight arrives white: every colour of the rainbow mixed together.
    draw sun l_sun noon_beam noon_you l_noon l_white

On its way down it hits air molecules, far smaller than a wavelength of light, and each knocks a little light aside.
    draw molecules parallel true

How much depends steeply on colour: scattering goes as one over the wavelength to the fourth power.
    draw ax ray l_ray

Blue, at about 450 nanometres, is scattered almost six times more than red at 700.
    dot p_blue #2f6b8f at.on ray at.x 450
    label l_blue "Blue" above-right attach_to p_blue
    dot p_red #b5482e at.on ray at.x 700
    label l_red "Red" above attach_to p_red

So wherever you look away from the sun, blue light is arriving from the side, scattered toward you.
    draw sky_scatter parallel true

That scattered blue is the sky.
    draw sky

Why not violet, which scatters even more?
    draw p_violet l_violet

The sun sends less violet, and our eyes are far less sensitive to it, so the mix looks blue.
    highlight p_violet l_violet

Now stand where the sun is setting: its light must cross far more air to reach you.
    draw dusk_you l_dusk dusk_beam

Near the horizon the path holds about thirty-eight times as much air as straight up, far more than this drawing can show.
    draw l_1x l_38x

Along that long path, blue is scattered out of the beam again and again.
    draw dusk_scatter parallel true

What reaches your eye is what is left: orange and red.
    draw dusk_2 dusk_3

So the blue sky and the red sunset are one effect: the blue knocked out of the beam, and the light that survives.
    focus sky_scatter noon_you dusk_scatter dusk_3 dusk_you earth

    quiz "The Moon has no air. What colour is its sky in the daytime?"
        right: Black: with no air there is nothing to scatter sunlight toward you, so you see only the sun itself.
        wrong: Ask what would send sunlight toward you from the empty sky.
        * Blue
        + Black
        * Red
---
